~~~ file: PoolToggle.svelte
<!--
  PoolToggle.svelte: an on/off switch whose knob is a little life ring floating across the water!

  <PoolToggle bind:checked={heated} label="Heated pool" />

  Props: checked (bindable), label (text next to it; or put words between the tags), disabled, onchange(checked), class.
  It is a real switch (role="switch"): Space and Enter flip it.
-->
<script>
    let { checked = $bindable(false), label = '', disabled = false, onchange = undefined, children = undefined, class: className = '' } = $props();
    const uid = 'plg' + Math.random().toString(36).slice(2, 8);
    function flip() {
        if (disabled) return;
        checked = !checked;
        if (typeof onchange === 'function') onchange(checked);
    }
</script>

<label class="pool-toggle {className}" class:on={checked} class:off-limits={disabled}>
    <button type="button" role="switch" aria-checked={checked} {disabled} onclick={flip} class="pool-track" aria-labelledby={label || children ? uid : undefined} aria-label={label || children ? undefined : 'Switch'}><span class="pool-ring" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
    {#if label || children}<span class="pool-toggle-label" id={uid}>{#if children}{@render children()}{:else}{label}{/if}</span>{/if}
</label>

<style>
    .pool-toggle { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; font: 600 14px var(--pool-font, system-ui, sans-serif); color: var(--pool-ink, #0c4a6e); cursor: pointer; }
    .off-limits { opacity: 0.5; cursor: not-allowed; }
    .pool-track { position: relative; width: 56px; height: 30px; flex: none; padding: 0; border-radius: 999px; cursor: inherit; border: 2px solid #94a3b8;
        background: #f1f5f9; box-sizing: border-box; transition: background 0.2s, border-color 0.2s; }
    .on .pool-track { border-color: var(--pool-water-3, #00b2e3);
        background: var(--pool-water-soft, #d6f4fc); }
    .pool-ring { position: absolute; top: 1px; left: 1px; width: 24px; height: 24px; border-radius: 50%; transition: left 0.22s cubic-bezier(.3, 1.4, .5, 1);
        background: conic-gradient(var(--pool-orange, #f97316) 0 45deg, #fff 45deg 90deg, var(--pool-orange, #f97316) 90deg 135deg, #fff 135deg 180deg, var(--pool-orange, #f97316) 180deg 225deg, #fff 225deg 270deg, var(--pool-orange, #f97316) 270deg 315deg, #fff 315deg);
        -webkit-mask: radial-gradient(circle, transparent 0 30%, #000 31%); mask: radial-gradient(circle, transparent 0 30%, #000 31%);
        filter: drop-shadow(0 0 0.7px rgba(154, 52, 18, 0.85)); }
    .on .pool-ring { left: 27px; }
    .pool-track:focus-visible { outline: 3px solid var(--pool-orange, #f97316); outline-offset: 2px; }
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { .pool-ring, .pool-track { transition: none; } }
</style>
~~~

~~~ file: PoolTooltip.svelte
<!--
  PoolTooltip.svelte: a little water bubble with a tip, shown when you point at (or tab to) something!

  <PoolTooltip tip="Lane 1 is the fast lane"><PoolButton>Lane 1</PoolButton></PoolTooltip>
  <PoolTooltip tip="3.8 metres!" place="bottom">deep end</PoolTooltip>

  Props: tip (the text), place ('top' default or 'bottom'), class. Wrap anything: when it is focusable (a button, a link),
  the tip follows its focus; plain words become focusable on their own. Escape hides the tip.
-->
<script>
    let { tip = '', place = 'top', children = undefined, class: className = '' } = $props();
    let shown = $state(false);
    let host = $state();
    const uid = 'plt' + Math.random().toString(36).slice(2, 8);
    // plain words get a tab stop; a button or link inside already has one, and gets the description
    let words = $state(true);
    $effect(() => {
        if (!host) return;
        const inner = host.querySelector('a[href], button, input, select, textarea, [tabindex]:not(.pool-tip)');
        words = !inner;
        if (inner) inner.setAttribute('aria-describedby', uid);
    });
</script>

<!-- (plain words need a tab stop so keyboard users can reach the tip) -->
<!-- svelte-ignore a11y_no_static_element_interactions, a11y_no_noninteractive_tabindex -->
<span class="pool-tip {className}" class:words bind:this={host} tabindex={words ? 0 : undefined} aria-describedby={words ? uid : undefined}
    onmouseenter={() => (shown = true)} onmouseleave={() => (shown = false)} onfocusin={() => (shown = true)} onfocusout={() => (shown = false)}
    onkeydown={(e) => { if (e.key === 'Escape') shown = false; }}>
    {#if children}{@render children()}{/if}
    <span class="pool-tip-bubble pool-{place}" class:on={shown} role="tooltip" id={uid}>{tip}</span>
</span>

<style>
    .pool-tip { position: relative; display: inline-block; outline: none; }
    .words { border-bottom: 2px dotted var(--pool-water-2, #22d3ee); cursor: help; }
    .words:focus-visible { background: rgba(34, 211, 238, 0.25); border-radius: 3px; }
    .pool-tip-bubble { position: absolute; left: 50%; z-index: 50; width: max-content; max-width: 260px; padding: 7px 12px; border-radius: 12px; pointer-events: none;
        font: 600 13px/1.4 var(--pool-font, system-ui, sans-serif); color: #fff; text-shadow: 0 1px 1px rgba(7, 89, 133, 0.5);
        background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.35) 0%, transparent 50%), linear-gradient(180deg, var(--pool-water-2, #22d3ee), var(--pool-water-3, #00b2e3));
        box-shadow: 0 6px 16px rgba(7, 89, 133, 0.3); opacity: 0; transition: opacity 0.15s, transform 0.15s; }
    .pool-tip-bubble::after { content: ''; position: absolute; left: 50%; width: 10px; height: 10px; margin-left: -5px; transform: rotate(45deg); background: var(--pool-water-3, #00b2e3); }
    .pool-top { bottom: calc(100% + 10px); transform: translate(-50%, 4px); box-shadow: inset 0 -3px 0 var(--pool-orange, #f97316), 0 6px 16px rgba(7, 89, 133, 0.3); }
    .pool-top::after { bottom: -5px; background: var(--pool-orange, #f97316); }
    .pool-bottom { top: calc(100% + 10px); transform: translate(-50%, -4px); box-shadow: inset 0 3px 0 var(--pool-orange, #f97316), 0 6px 16px rgba(7, 89, 133, 0.3); }
    .pool-bottom::after { top: -5px; background: var(--pool-orange, #f97316); }
    .pool-tip-bubble.on { opacity: 1; transform: translate(-50%, 0); }
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { .pool-tip-bubble { transition: none; } }
</style>
~~~

~~~ file: poolside.css
/* PoolsideUI design tokens (optional): every component has these built in as fallbacks.
   Load this file (or set any of these on a parent) to recolor the whole set at once!
   The Poolside rule: clear water (cyan to blue) for surfaces, orange only as a crisp accent
   (stripes, edges, rings, tips), never blended into the water in one gradient. */
:root {
    --pool-water-1: #67e8f9;   /* sunny shallow water */
    --pool-water-2: #22d3ee;
    --pool-water-3: #00b2e3;   /* the deep end: a vivid cyan (darker cyans turn teal, bluer ones turn Aero) */
    --pool-deep: #075985;      /* text on light water */
    --pool-ink: #0c4a6e;       /* body text */
    --pool-orange: #f97316;    /* life rings, lane ropes, stripes */
    --pool-orange-deep: #c2410c;
    --pool-water-soft: #d6f4fc;  /* the light fill of a flat button (its border is the main colour) */
    --pool-orange-soft: #ffe9d6;
    --pool-tile: #f0fdff;      /* white pool tiles */
    --pool-tile-line: #cff4fc;
    --pool-line: rgba(14, 165, 233, 0.4);
    --pool-shadow: rgba(8, 145, 178, 0.22);
    --pool-radius: 16px;
    --pool-font: "Segoe UI", system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif;
}
~~~

~~~ file: README.md
# PoolsideUI

Twenty-six Svelte 5 components in the Poolside style: clear water from cyan to blue, with orange as a crisp accent
(stripes, edges, life rings, lane ropes), never blended into the water.

| Component | What it is |
| --- | --- |
| `PoolButton` | Flat water, orange (life ring) or ghost button: the main colour is the border, a lighter shade is the fill, with a ripple; sizes, links, disabled |
| `PoolCard` | Tile card with a rippling water header, orange stripe, life-ring icon, footer snippet, or `flat` |
| `PoolToggle` | Switch (`role="switch"`) whose knob is a life ring; `bind:checked` |
| `PoolSlider` | Range slider that fills with water up to an orange float; `bind:value`, label, unit |
| `PoolProgress` | Water-level progress as a bar or a round porthole with waves; no value means busy |
| `PoolTabs` | Lane tabs split by orange-and-white lane ropes; `bind:active`, `panel` snippet, arrow keys |
| `PoolInput` | Text field or text area with a water focus ring, hint, and orange error message |
| `PoolChip` | Pill in water, orange or soft, removable with `onremove` |
| `PoolDialog` | Modal on the native `<dialog>`; `bind:open`, title, footer snippet, Escape and backdrop close |
| `PoolToaster` | Bubble messages: put one `<PoolToaster />` on the page, then `toast('Saved!')` from anywhere |
| `PoolAccordion` | Questions that open one at a time (or `multiple`), orange edge and arrow |
| `PoolTiles` | Section backdrop of pool tiles with drifting light and a lane rope; `depth="deep"` |
| `PoolCheckbox` | Checkbox that fills with water, orange-shadowed tick, `indeterminate` dash; `bind:checked` |
| `PoolRadioGroup` | Pick one: floats with an orange center; strings or `{ value, label, hint, disabled }`, `row` |
| `PoolSelect` | The browser's own drop-down styled like PoolInput, orange arrow, placeholder, hint, error |
| `PoolSegmented` | Joined buttons with a sliding water bubble; arrow keys |
| `PoolAlert` | Banner: info, success, warning (orange edge), danger; `dismissible`, `actions` snippet |
| `PoolSpinner` | A spinning life ring (pulses with reduced motion) |
| `PoolSkeleton` | Loading stand-ins (text lines, circle, block) with a sunlight shimmer |
| `PoolTooltip` | Water tip bubble on hover or focus; wraps buttons, links or plain words |
| `PoolAvatar` | Porthole with initials or a picture, orange ring, status float |
| `PoolMenu` | Button with a drop-down menu of actions; full keyboard support, separators, danger items |
| `PoolStepper` | Steps along a lane rope; click a done step to go back |
| `PoolPagination` | Page floats with "…" gaps |
| `PoolTable` | Water header row, tile stripes, click-to-sort columns with `aria-sort`, formatters |
| `PoolStat` | Dashboard number tile with change (up in blue, down in orange) and a small trend line |

Every component has its colors built in. `poolside.css` holds the same tokens (`--pool-water-1` … `--pool-orange`),
so loading it, or setting them on a parent, recolors the whole set. Everything works with the keyboard and screen
readers, and animations stop when the system asks for reduced motion.

```svelte
<script>
    import { PoolButton, PoolCard, PoolToaster, toast } from './PoolsideUI/index.js';
</script>

<PoolToaster />
<PoolCard title="Pool party" subtitle="Saturday">
    Bring a towel!
    {#snippet footer()}<PoolButton size="small" onclick={() => toast("See you there!")}>I'm coming!</PoolButton>{/snippet}
</PoolCard>
```

**Demo:** `cd demo && node build.mjs`, then open `demo/index.html`!

**Flat buttons:** buttons and button-like controls (`PoolButton`, `PoolChip`, `PoolToggle`, `PoolSegmented`, `PoolTabs`, `PoolPagination`, `PoolStepper`, `PoolCheckbox`, `PoolRadioGroup` and the items of `PoolMenu`) are flat: the main colour is the border and a lighter shade of it is the fill (`--pool-water-soft` and `--pool-orange-soft` in `poolside.css`). The other components keep their water headers, tiles and shadows.
~~~
